        {"objects": [{"type":"dynamic","data":{"position":{"x":3,"y":1},"name":"show_text_fullscreen","options":{"text":
            "(Mr. Bennet approaches Mr. Darcy)\nMr. Bennet: Mr. Darcy!\nMr. Darcy: Why Mr. Bennet, what brings you to /gLondon on this fine cloudy day?\nMr. Bennet: Lydia ran off with Wickham and they are planning to leave the country! Have you any information on their whereabouts?\nMr. Darcy: Oh my! Indeed I do, I can bring you to them immediately.\nMr. Bennet: Thank you, sir!\nMr. Darcy: Although, I don’t believe we can keep Wickham in the country without some incentive…\nMr. Bennet: Well, if we force him to actually marry Lydia, there’s nothing he can do to get away, and he won’t be able to harm any more women!\nMr. Darcy: It’s settled then, we shall approach him, you will get your revenge and I will pay him off to get him to marry Lydia and get him to stay in the country."
        }}}]},
